# GirGuard AI — Frontend Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values for your environment.
# NEVER commit .env.local to git.
# NEVER put IBM API keys or secrets in any frontend .env file.
#
# ── Backend API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this to connect the frontend to the Flask backend.
# Leave empty (or unset) to use mock data (demo mode).
#
# Local development:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/v1
#
# IBM Cloud deployment (Task 3):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-ibm-cloud-backend.example.com/api/v1
#
# ── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IBM Granite / WatsonX API keys must ONLY exist in the Flask backend.
# The browser frontend must NEVER hold private IBM Cloud credentials.
